# Offline bundle manifest

What `gather-bundle.sh` puts on the flashdrive, and why. The guiding rule: the
bundle carries ONLY what a fresh, offline box cannot fetch for itself — i.e. just
enough to get wifi up. Once online, the box downloads everything else (documented
in NEW-DEVICE.md), so it is never stale on the flash.

## In the bundle (`home-server-bundle/`)

- **`wifi-debs/`** — the wifi userspace, as `.deb`s for the target's Debian release
  (trixie). This is the cold-start unblock: a bare Proxmox box has no wifi client,
  so it cannot apt-install one without internet it doesn't have yet.
  - Generic WPA stack (hardware-independent): `wpasupplicant`, `iw`, `rfkill`,
    `wireless-regdb`, and wpasupplicant's non-base deps `libnl-3-200`,
    `libnl-genl-3-200`, `libnl-route-3-200`, `libpcsclite1`.
  - Common wifi-chip firmware (device-specific, best-effort): `firmware-iwlwifi`,
    `firmware-realtek`, `firmware-misc-nonfree`. Often already present in the
    Proxmox install (the first box's AX200 was), but bundled so a *different*
    laptop's chip is covered.
- **`home-server-repo.tar.gz`** — a pristine snapshot of this repo at HEAD. Carries
  `first-contact.sh` and `bootstrap.sh` themselves, so the box needs nothing from
  the network to start. Extracts to `/srv/dev/repos/home-server`.
- **`NEW-DEVICE.md`**, **`offline-bundle.manifest`** — this runbook + list, for
  reference at the keyboard.

## Deliberately NOT in the bundle (fetched once online)

- **Proxmox VE ISO** — installed from its own USB before any of this; separate.
- **Debian cloud image** for the Valheim VM — `guests/create-valheim-vm.sh` pulls it.
- **Node.js + Claude Code** — installed after first-contact (native installer).
- **Valheim mods** — fetched/staged by `valheim/stage-mods.sh` per `valheim/mods.manifest`.
- **Secrets** — `backup.env`, `valheim.env`; created by hand, never on the flash.

## Refreshing the bundle

Re-run `gather-bundle.sh` whenever the repo changes or the target Debian release
changes. The `.debs` must match the target release, so run it on a box of that
release (trixie for Proxmox 9).
